{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/799073-raising-the-level-of-a-power-and-buying-an-extra-help-pls","id":799073,"title":"Raising the level of a power and buying an extra (Help pls)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T22:51:16-08:00","id":799073,"title":"Raising the level of a power and buying an extra (Help pls)","content":"Ok using the rules from the first edition Aberrant game drawn from the core book, the players guide, and the biomanipulation power from Worldwide Phase I. Say I have a Quantum of 6 and I decide to buy Biomanipulation a level 3 power. I buy it at 2 ranks with the extra affect microbes....<br /> <br /> Because I have a Q6 the extra costs me 7xp (a lvl 3 current cost to raise (hope I got that right sorta confused on that cost) but it doesn't raise the level of the power since my Quantum level lets me set two extra before raising the level.<br /> <br /> Now a few weeks later I've earned the 5 xp I need to master the power (I already have the power at 2 ranks which cost me 16xp. The cost of the same power mastered is 21.... a difference of 5...<br /> <br /> Mastery raised the level of the power from 3 to 4, at a Q of 6 a Lvl 4 power raises another level with just one extra.... so is my old affects microbes grandfathered in and ignored or do I lose the extra or can I not even master the power because I bought the damn extra ?<br /> <br /> Any help appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T04:59:27-08:00","id":799530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/799073-raising-the-level-of-a-power-and-buying-an-extra-help-pls#post799073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok using the rules from the first edition Aberrant game drawn from the core book, the players guide, and the biomanipulation power from Worldwide Phase I. Say I have a Quantum of 6 and I decide to buy Biomanipulation a level 3 power. I buy it at 2 ranks with the extra affect microbes....<br /> <br /> Because I have a Q6 the extra costs me 7xp (a lvl 3 current cost to raise (hope I got that right sorta confused on that cost) but it doesn't raise the level of the power since my Quantum level lets me set two extra before raising the level.<br /> <br /> Now a few weeks later I've earned the 5 xp I need to master the power (I already have the power at 2 ranks which cost me 16xp. The cost of the same power mastered is 21.... a difference of 5...<br /> <br /> Mastery raised the level of the power from 3 to 4, at a Q of 6 a Lvl 4 power raises another level with just one extra.... so is my old affects microbes grandfathered in and ignored or do I lose the extra or can I not even master the power because I bought the damn extra ?<br /> <br /> Any help appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the first case applies, as it is never actually stated Mastery costs extra slots, impedes Q6+ Novas of acquiring other extras beforehand or anything like that, only that purchasing it auto-raises the level of a power, so purchasing both should be ok as long as Mastery is the final addition, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user"